  "proofIdea": "Take integral left-division matrices whose odd-prime reductions are actual division images of the source. Every identity of those finite images holds over the integers, since a nonzero integer cannot vanish modulo every sufficiently large prime. A surjective map modulo 2 sends the integral operation to two-element left zero. Left zero has no left division, contradicting an exact image characterization. For E907 the opposite right-division matrices are integral as well, giving the other-side obstruction. The same transfer excludes a uniform reverse term on these families.",
