  "researchOnly": {
    "E872": "Still only the previously proved two-equation basis. 140 further unit-insertion candidates produced no ATP proof; 138 tested candidates, including earlier simple insertions, have explicit countermodels of orders 2\u20135. Another 53 composite identities were refuted under the left-quasigroup restriction. Compound-vs-compound identities cannot themselves exclude constant magmas.",
    "E1518": "Adding the explicit inverse-composition and square-bijection identities did not produce a square-cube proof within the five-minute Vampire run. The finite uniform-term question remains open.",
    "E1286": "A seven-operation relation obtained by rotating constraints is insufficient as an unconditional characterization: the two-element constant magma satisfies it.",
    "noncommutingMatrixSearch": "Exhaustively tested 19,494,848 noncommuting 2x2 pairs with entries in [-5,5], Q determinant in {+/-2,+/-4,+/-8}, and a common one-dimensional singular reduction modulo 2 against the open representative laws. No additional family found. At bad primes 3 and 5, analogous searches tested 6,315,488 and 4,116,080 pairs respectively and found no additional family.",
